# --- brace-expansion DoS (CVE-2026-14257), via puppeteer-extra-plugin-
# stealth -> puppeteer-extra-plugin-user-data-dir -> rimraf@3 -> glob@7 ->
# minimatch@3 -> brace-expansion@1.1.16. No fixed 1.x release exists — the
# only patch is brace-expansion@5.0.8, a rewrite with an incompatible API
# (1.x: `module.exports = expandTop`, callable directly; 5.x: named exports
# `{ expand, ... }`) that minimatch@3.1.5 calls as a function. Forcing 5.x
# via npm overrides would silently break minimatch's glob matching — worse
# than the vulnerability itself. And the vulnerability requires
# attacker-controlled input reaching brace-expansion.expand(); here it's
# only ever invoked internally (temp directory cleanup), never on data from
# an HTTP request, so the real-world exploitability is effectively nil.
# Revisit once puppeteer-extra-plugin-user-data-dir ships a newer major.
CVE-2026-14257
